{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1304046-craftwork-what-qualifies","id":1304046,"title":"Craftwork - what qualifies?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-10T16:58:27-07:00","id":1304046,"title":"Craftwork - what qualifies?","content":"Question for the court. Boggans have the Craftwork birthright, which is one of several among the various kiths that cut down on time for physical labor. However, it is a bit unclear what would qualify. Does it have to be something primarily physical - cleaning, building, farming - or could a task of mixed duties work - typing a report, but the binding and distributing the report?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T17:59:50-07:00","id":1304054,"title":"","content":"It is supposed to include things like baking/cooking, sewing, and the like, so, personally, I'd allow traditional &quot;clerk/secretary&quot; type office work, as well as redecorating, butler/maid activities, and certain trades. I think, for me, I just have to have a sense of what feels &quot;right&quot; and what is iffy or a bridge too far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T18:12:23-07:00","id":1304058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1304046-craftwork-what-qualifies?p=1304054#post1304054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is supposed to include things like baking/cooking, sewing, and the like, so, personally, I'd allow traditional &quot;clerk/secretary&quot; type office work, as well as redecorating, butler/maid activities, and certain trades. I think, for me, I just have to have a sense of what feels &quot;right&quot; and what is iffy or a bridge too far.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was kind of my thought too. To a certain extent, it all is somewhat physical, but it seems more oriented towards &quot;things that can be done to help other people,&quot; or else &quot;entry level&quot; tasks versus more intellectual pursuits (research and writing could work if done as a &quot;task&quot; might fit, but not just looking around for arcane secrets for yourself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T02:21:12-07:00","id":1304132,"title":"","content":"I'd say writing a report counts, given the bogans I've worked with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T12:25:37-07:00","id":1304288,"title":"","content":"I would be hard pressed to say what doesn't count. If there's no human contact involved, directly or online, then you work fast.<br /> <br /> Now here's a more interesting question. The rules say you must be unobserved. Does that count Google? What about advertising trackers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T14:31:24-07:00","id":1304321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1304046-craftwork-what-qualifies?p=1304288#post1304288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would be hard pressed to say what doesn't count. If there's no human contact involved, directly or online, then you work fast.<br /> <br /> Now here's a more interesting question. The rules say you must be unobserved. Does that count Google? What about advertising trackers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm. Good question. Security cameras did count against pookas.... but the thing with those is, either someone is watching on the other end or someone can go back and watch easily. Technically someone can go through Google's history manually and find what you did... but that isn't actually thepoint of it.the point is to track you for relevant ads.<br /> So my ruling is, you won't be hit by that unless someone is actively hafcling you. Alternatively, use incognito window.<br /> <br /> ....it occurs to me 5hat the boggans probably invented a browser/ad blocker for just that issue...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T16:50:54-07:00","id":1304340,"title":"","content":"What I do know is messaging them on Skype *definitely* breaks the Birthright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T18:06:31-07:00","id":1304356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1304046-craftwork-what-qualifies?p=1304321#post1304321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmmm. Good question. Security cameras did count against pookas....</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd always just handwaved it that the Mists conspired to make most mortal technologies glitch in a way that kept the existence of the fey unproveable and inconclusive. Not quite as blunt as what you see in, say, Frailty, but similar in concept.<br /> <br /> Also, I always houseruled that Craftwork worked perfectly fine around other Boggins, so that they could work together.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T18:08:12-07:00","id":1304357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1304046-craftwork-what-qualifies?p=1304356#post1304356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd always just handwaved it that the Mists conspired to make most mortal technologies glitch in a way that kept the existence of the fey unproveable and inconclusive. Not quite as blunt as what you see in, say, Frailty, but similar in concept.<br /> <br /> Also, I always houseruled that Craftwork worked perfectly fine around other Boggins, so that they could work together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that the Boggans thing is canon in at least one iteration... they can work together on something to go more quickly (see: the Seven Dwarves of Disney)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-11T22:18:35-07:00","id":1304397,"title":"","content":"The Boggan Birthright outright states that other Boggan may be present but no other observers. At least in C20 but I recall always playing them thus so it is likely that it has always been so, though apparently that is not directly mentioned in 2nd ed core book... wow. Seems I too have always Houseruled it working fine with other Boggans around untill now that C20 has made it into an actual rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T10:43:45-07:00","id":1304464,"title":"","content":"I don't count machines that lack &quot;personhood&quot; Now that Inanimae that lives in videogames.. he counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T06:47:07-07:00","id":1304615,"title":"","content":"I would have gone the other way and said that Boggans who work online are the most conscientious about blocking trackers, using startpage instead of google and generally locking down equipment so nobody can watch them. It's just part of what makes them feel comfortable so their birthright can kick in.<br /> <br /> If you want to know why then you're a bigger intrusion than possible spyware so shoo along now. Shoo. I've got work to get done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-13T11:58:26-07:00","id":1304654,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit unsure about the line between the personality of a strongly technical in a computer sense boggan and nocker. I guess using well established and vetted tools while being paranoid about security would be the boggan method, while a nocker might end up writing their own browser and whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T04:13:42-07:00","id":1304777,"title":"","content":"The main difference between a nocker and a boggan is that the boggan pays lip service to the laws of physics. A nocker working online would be using a brain interface or a holographic display (hard light, obviously) while a boggan would be typing really fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T10:47:51-07:00","id":1305085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1304046-craftwork-what-qualifies?p=1304777#post1304777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main difference between a nocker and a boggan is that the boggan pays lip service to the laws of physics. A nocker working online would be using a brain interface or a holographic display (hard light, obviously) while a boggan would be typing really fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would you support that mechanically at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-15T15:24:03-07:00","id":1305151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1304046-craftwork-what-qualifies?p=1305085#post1305085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would you support that mechanically at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, from my experience with Nockers, I'd probably start with the stats for a frag grenade...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-16T10:27:55-07:00","id":1305296,"title":"","content":"Mechanically I would say the Nocker makes a craft roll as described in his birthright to build an impromptu hard light interface. Six rusty nails, half a bottle of Cherry Chouffe, a green lightbulb and two wire coathangers poked into a telephone socket provide him with an internet connected terminal.<br /> <br /> With a poor roll his terminal comes with a penalty to Computer, with a very good roll it provides some small bonus. Either way the frailty still applies, at a key moment it has a 10% chance of breaking.<br /> <br /> The Boggan meanwhile just gets a speed bonus. Looking up the family tree of the house of Grimaldi on his iphone is normal difficulty, looking up the family tree of the house of Grimaldi in time to make a crucial phone call to prevent an execution is also normal difficulty because unlike everyone else there's plenty of time for a Boggan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13395,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","user":"Daniel Knight","date":". 04-16-2019, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T08:02:31-07:00","id":1305477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1304046-craftwork-what-qualifies?p=1304356#post1304356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd always just handwaved it that the Mists conspired to make most mortal technologies glitch in a way that kept the existence of the fey unproveable and inconclusive. Not quite as blunt as what you see in, say, Frailty, but similar in concept.<br /> <br /> Also, I always houseruled that Craftwork worked perfectly fine around other Boggins, so that they could work together.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It helps that the fae often innovate and invent their own brand of magitech and ephemeral electronics. <br /> <br /> ::whistles and walks away::","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Luka Carroll</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer &amp; Developer<br /> <i>Working On: </i>C20 Player's Guide, Lunars<br /> <i>Worked On: </i>V20 TMR, Demon STG, C20, Book of Freeholds, Conquering Heroes, Building A Legend, Dragon-Blooded, The Realm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3785-luka-c","name":"Luka C","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3785_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-17T18:49:07-07:00","id":1305617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Luka C</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1304046-craftwork-what-qualifies?p=1305477#post1305477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It helps that the fae often innovate and invent their own brand of magitech and ephemeral electronics.<br /> <br /> ::whistles and walks away::</div> </div> </div> </div>I've long wanted to see a book about Changelings and technology and science fiction related topics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}